From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Mason <jon.mason@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:27:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rse: match MCUboot's key hash callback

The RSE BL2 implementation still passes a key index to this callback, but
MCUboot 2.4 only passes the image index when multi-signature support is
disabled. Match the callback declaration for the TC3 configuration.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jon Mason <jon.mason@arm.com>
---
 platform/ext/target/arm/rse/common/bl2/rse_bl2_rotpk.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/ext/target/arm/rse/common/bl2/rse_bl2_rotpk.c b/platform/ext/target/arm/rse/common/bl2/rse_bl2_rotpk.c
index 8e5a997..2e5f88a 100644
--- a/platform/ext/target/arm/rse/common/bl2/rse_bl2_rotpk.c
+++ b/platform/ext/target/arm/rse/common/bl2/rse_bl2_rotpk.c
@@ -82,4 +82,3 @@
 int boot_retrieve_public_key_hash(uint8_t image_index,
-                                  uint8_t key_index,
                                   uint8_t *public_key_hash,
                                   size_t *key_hash_size)
@@ -86,4 +85,3 @@
 {
-    (void)key_index;
     enum tfm_otp_element_id_t otp_id;
     enum tfm_plat_err_t err;
